# Split from server.lang - dialogue bundle (aetherhaven_dialogue_logger)
# Full translation keys are aetherhaven_dialogue_logger.<lineKey> (see Hytale I18nModule).
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.rep_reward_50.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.rep_reward_100.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.root.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.root.body=I fell trees and process them into lumber for the settlement. This work becomes much more precise when we have an actual lumbermill with proper saws, stacking space, and a dedicated bench. If you build that for me, I can keep the plank racks full instead of leaving good timber in messy piles outside the walls. I need sharp iron and straight boards; that is how I operate.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.root.hc0=You wanted to talk about a house.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.root.hc1=I house is ready for you. I wanted you to hear it from me directly.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.root.hc2=The house is still in progress.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.root.c0=I wanted to follow up now that your lumbermill is built.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.root.c1=The lumbermill is complete. I am ready to close out the quest.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.root.c2=The mill is only partly built so far. I wanted to ask how that is going.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.root.c3=I want to help you get a lumbermill. Can we start with the plot and token?
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.root.c4=That is all for now. I will talk to you later.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_quest_mill.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_quest_mill.body=Give me the token and a staked plot for the mill, and I will take ownership of the construction immediately. Once the roof is sealed and the bench is installed, I will begin processing logs so the town receives clean, stacked lumber from production storage.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_quest_mill.c0=Here is the token. I will get the mill built.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_quest_mill.c1=I am not ready to commit to that yet.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_accepted.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_accepted.body=Perfect. Once the shell is sealed against the weather, I will meet you at the mill desk. I want to show you exactly how the intake and output systems are laid out.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_accepted.c0=Sounds good. I will see you when the mill is ready.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_building.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_building.body=The construction sign still lists missing items. Please finish delivering what it asks for, or tell me clearly if you are abandoning the mill.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_building.c0=I need to stop this build and abandon the project.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_building.c1=I am still building and I will finish the mill.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_abandoned.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_abandoned.body=Understood. I won't be able to produce any materials until the mill is finished, so let me know when you're ready try again.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_abandoned.c0=All right. I will see you around.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_done.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_done.body=Now that the mill is running, I can cut and keep cordwood and logs in storage. If you need more processed wood, check with me at the bench, and we will organize what the storerooms need next.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_done.c0=Thanks. I will let you know if we run low on wood.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_offer.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_offer.body=There's nothing comfortable about sleeping in a workshop. I want a regular house plot like the rest of the town.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_offer.c0=I will stake the house and get it built.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_offer.c1=Another time.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_accepted.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_accepted.body=When the shell is weather-tight, register me on the bookshelf, then come see me here so you can hand me the keys.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_accepted.c0=You will hear it from me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_remind.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_remind.body=Finish the frame when you can. Register me when the block is ready. I will keep cutting at the mill while you work on the house.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_remind.c0=Understood.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_finish.speaker=Seren Fairhollow
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_finish.body=Good. Now I can leave the sawdust at work instead of shaking it out of my blanket at the inn.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.seren_house_finish.c0=Enjoy the quiet roof.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.gift.love=This is excellent stock for my work. It is the kind of gift that makes tomorrow significantly easier. Thank you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.gift.like=That is a thoughtful thing to bring. I will put it straight into the workflow here.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.gift.neutral=I will tuck that away for now and find a sensible place for it once I see what the week brings.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.gift.dislike=I spend my days working with timber, so a stack of stone blocks is not useful to me. But the miner's hut could always use more.

aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.fallback=If you need the mill, updates on the house, or clean boards for the storerooms, let me know.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.greeting.0=Mind your step. If you kick up the sawdust, it will get everywhere. And I mean everywhere.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.greeting.1=Hello! I'm between jobs, so I have a moment. Did you have a question?
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.greeting.2=A little wisdom for you: Wind in the rafters is normal, but loud cracks are not. Always listen for trouble.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.greeting.3=You're just in time. I just finished an order and my slate is clean. What do you need?
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.greeting.4=Neat piles of logs and lumber always improve my mood.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.greeting.5=If you hear the mill singing, it is happy. If it groans, be extra careful.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.greeting.6=Mud happens during storms. Just brush it off before you touch the dry stock.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.greeting.7=If you can bring me samples of timber that I don't have in stock, I can see about sourcing more. Look at the stockpile to place an order.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.greeting.8=Tell me what you are building before you ask for specific product. I can make sure you get exactly what's best for it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.greeting.9=I prefer short questions when the saws are hungry for timber.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.hint.love.0=Straight grain and clean cordwood tell me you understand timber quality.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.hint.love.1=I notice immediately when someone brings tools that respect a sharp edge.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.hint.love.2=A good meal after a long day of cutting lands better than fancy words.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.hint.love.3=If you bring nails and brackets that match real joinery work, I appreciate the effort.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.hint.love.4=I prefer gifts that belong in a dry shed, not in a parlor.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.hint.dislike.0=I'm not interested in stone, but the miner might like some.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.hint.dislike.1=Someone tried to give me a bag of bones earlier. I threw them out of my shop.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.hint.dislike.2=If anything in your bag is rotten or slimy, keep it far away from the timber.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.hint.dislike.3=Please do not try to peddle off trash scrap with me. I'm in a good rhythm and it will only distract me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.main_hub.hint.dislike.4=Don't try to flatter me with glittery junk.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.birthday.greeting=A birthday in the forest air. Glad you came to say hello.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.gift.love.birthday=It is my birthday and this gift is wonderful. You made my whole day.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.gift.like.birthday=A birthday gift like this. You have good taste.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.gift.neutral.birthday=Thanks. A simple gift on my birthday still means a lot.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_logger.gift.dislike.birthday=It is my birthday and you brought that. Well. I still appreciate the thought.
